# {{title}}: notes for coding agents

A [Renox](https://github.com/arif-rachim/renox) app: Rust + Axum + HTMX + Alpine.js, like Laravel.
The framework is the `renox` dependency; don't copy its code into this app.

## How to do things

Check the Renox cheat-sheet first. It has one short, compiled example per task: routes, views,
forms and validation, models, queries, pagination, auth and policies, HTMX, jobs, mail, cache,
uploads, tests.
- https://github.com/arif-rachim/renox/blob/main/CHEATSHEET.md
- Local copy: in the `renox` checkout Cargo downloaded (`~/.cargo/git/checkouts/renox-*/*/`),
  next to `llms.txt`, which lists complete example apps such as `examples/crud`.

Prefer the generators over writing boilerplate by hand:

```bash
rnx make:module products                               # src/app/products + view + registration
rnx make:model Product --module products --migration   # model + migrations/*.sql
rnx make:policy Product --module products
rnx make:job SendReceipt --module products
rnx make:mail order_shipped
rnx make:migration add_stock_to_products
```

## Layout

- `src/lib.rs`: `app()` builds the App (modules, migrations, seeders); `src/main.rs` only runs it.
- `src/app/<module>/mod.rs`: one module per feature (routes + handlers), with `model.rs`,
  `policy.rs` and jobs next to it.
- `resources/views/`: MiniJinja templates (`layouts/app.html` is the layout).
  `resources/lang/*.json`: translations. `public/`: static files.
- `migrations/`: `TIMESTAMP_name.up.sql` / `.down.sql`, written for the database in
  `DATABASE_URL` (`.env`).
- `tests/`: integration tests with `renox::testing::TestApp`.

## Checks before you finish

```bash
cargo test            # boots the app on a fresh test database
cargo clippy --all-targets
rnx route:list        # confirm routes and their names
```

Run the app with `rnx serve` (it rebuilds on changes) and try pages at http://127.0.0.1:3000.
